{"Images": [{"Name": "i0", "Description": "Diabetic nephropathy (DN)", "Path": "images/DN-artery", "Width": 1405, "Height": 1324, "MaxLevel": 1}], "Header": "**Diabetic nephropathy** is one of the most commun causes of chronic kidney disease. The glomerulus is its primary target. Early changes include glomerular hyperfiltration and progressive podocyte injury. \n\nAlthough vascular dysfunction is an important component of DN pathophysiology, arterial structures may remain relatively preserved depending on the stage and severity of the disease. In this context, the renal arteries can serve as internal structural references for the assessment of vascular markers and endothelial integrity. ", "Rotation": 0, "Layout": {"Grid": [["i0"]]}, "Stories": [{"Name": "", "Description": "", "Waypoints": [{"Name": "Structure of the artery", "Description": "The renal artery plays a critical role in maintaining kidney perfusion and delivering oxygen and nutrients to renal tissues. Its vascular wall is composed of endothelial cells lining the lumen and smooth muscle cells that regulate blood flow. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Artery", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.5305891238670865, 0.4539517455735279]}, {"Name": "Complement activation", "Description": "The complement is a part of the immune system. It can be activated by three different pathways : the classical, lectin or alternative pathway. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Classical complement pathway", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.5305891238670696, 0.4539517455735279]}, {"Name": "Complement activation pt. 2", "Description": "MBL acts like C1q in the lectin pathway : it is necessary to initiate the complement cascade activation. It recognizes sugar patterns on pathogens and allows the formation of the C3 convertase. Here, there is not a lot of MBL deposit, suggesting that that pathway is not activated. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Lectin complement pathway", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.5305891238670696, 0.4539517455735279]}, {"Name": "Complement activation pt. 3", "Description": "Only a few C1q - antibodies complexes are observed, which would suggest that the classical pathway is slightly activated. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Complement - antibodies complexes", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.5305891238670696, 0.4539517455735279]}, {"Name": "Terminal pathway", "Description": "There is very few deposition of C9 within the artery, indicating that the **membrane attack complex (MAC)** is not efficiently formed. ", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Activated complement", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.5305891238670694, 0.47346632052169235]}, {"Name": "Immune infiltration", "Description": "The activation of the complement leads to the formation of two anaphylatoxins, C3a and C5a, whose role is to recruit immune cells to sites of complement activation. Here, there is very no immune infiltration of lymphocytes (CD3 and CD20) and no other immune cells seem to detected (apart from one).", "Arrows": [{"Text": "", "HideArrow": false, "Point": [0.062010859573820465, 0.5171530448986348], "Angle": 60}], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Immune cells", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.5124375000000001, "Pan": [0.29872559797758147, 0.5075387190508632]}, {"Name": "Macrophage infiltration", "Description": "Macrophage infiltration is not really observed in the tissue, as the staining seem to be more of an artefact.", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Macrophages", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.5084340820312501, "Pan": [0.29872559797758147, 0.5075387190508632]}, {"Name": "Myeloid infiltration", "Description": "These findings indicate that there is no innate immune response due to complement activation within the tissue.", "Arrows": [], "Overlays": [], "Group": "Myeloid cells", "Masks": [], "ActiveMasks": [], "Zoom": 0.4270312500000001, "Pan": [0.5305891238670783, 0.2792884249509977]}]}], "Channels": [{"Rendered": false, "Name": "DAPI", "Path": "DAPI_0__DAPI"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "Megalin", "Path": "Megalin_24__Megalin"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "VCAM1", "Path": "VCAM1_21__VCAM1"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD31", "Path": "CD31_23__CD31"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "aSMA", "Path": "aSMA_19__aSMA"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C1q", "Path": "C1q_3__C1q"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C1r", "Path": "C1r_12__C1r"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C1s", "Path": "C1s_14__C1s"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "MBL", "Path": "MBL_17__MBL"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "IgG", "Path": "IgG_26__IgG"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C3c", "Path": "C3c_8__C3c"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C3d", "Path": "C3d_10__C3d"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C4d", "Path": "C4d_16__C4d"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C9", "Path": "C9_18__C9"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD45", "Path": "CD45_11__CD45"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD20", "Path": "CD20_13__CD20"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD3", "Path": "CD3_20__CD3"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "Ki67", "Path": "Ki67_15__Ki67"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD68", "Path": "CD68_7__CD68"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD163", "Path": "CD163_9__CD163"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "C5aR1", "Path": "C5aR1_6__C5aR1"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "CD11b", "Path": "CD11b_22__CD11b"}, {"Rendered": false, "Name": "MPO", "Path": "MPO_25__MPO"}], "Masks": [], "Groups": [{"Name": "Artery", "Colors": ["0000ff", "ffff00", "870a0a", "ffffff", "077507"], "Channels": ["DAPI", "Megalin", "VCAM1", "CD31", "aSMA"], "Descriptions": ["DNA", "Proximal tubules", "Endothelium", "Endothelium", "Blood vessels"]}, {"Name": "Classical complement pathway", "Colors": ["0000ff", "ffff00", "00ffff", "ff00ff", "077507", "ffffff"], "Channels": ["DAPI", "C1q", "C1r", "C1s", "aSMA", "CD31"], 